  "body": "**Research note (structural pricing screen); no \u03ba claim.** [#2435](https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/pull/2435) (Jeremy Kothe) gains +1.3164e-6 by raising 24 copy-buffer entrance frames per word from dimension 1 to 2. The change is frame-only (#2446). This note decomposes it per register and prices further raises of the same structural kind.\n\n1. **It is a width exchange paid for by the partners.** In both providers, 96 registers' climbs change.\n   - **The 24 raised helpers** each go from a rank-3 child to rank 2, and from width 8 to 7.\n   - **72 gate partners** (6 X registers, 66 helpers) each split a rank-3 child into rank 2 + rank 1, which is locally worse.\n   - The net gain is mainly packing: width-7 helpers fill the rank-16 bins as [7, 9].\n2. **Calibration.** The width-aware bin-pattern LP (#2387/#2360/#1129) moves the ceiling by **+1.3166e-6** from #2322 to #2435. The realized \u03ba gain is +1.3164e-6.\n3. **Further raises at #2435's point** (k raises, each width 8 \u2192 7):\n\n| k | average #2435 pattern, partners included | own climb only, no partner splits |\n|---|---|---|\n| 1 | +3.05e-8 | +3.84e-7 |\n| 10 | **+3.05e-7 (peak)** | +3.85e-6 |\n| 12 | +9.6e-8 | **+4.35e-6 (peak)** |\n| 16 | \u22121.40e-6 | +4.26e-6 |\n| 26 | \u22126.02e-6 | +3.15e-6 |\n\n   - With average partner costs the lever saturates after about 10 more raises, at about +3e-7, and then packing turns it negative.\n   - Partner splits consume about 92% of each raise's value. Raises without partner splits are about 12\u00d7 more valuable.\n4. **Census of remaining sites.**\n   - 112 dimension-1 entrances remain. Their (width, first climb) shapes are {(7,2): 30, (8,2): 26, (8,3): 52, (8,4): 4}, so 26 share the shape of #2435's 24.\n   - Every one of them has its first gate at the entrance frame, and only 16 have those gates in A alone. Further raises therefore need a joint frame re-solve that treats entrances as variables.\n\n**Checks.**\n- The recounts of the four pinned words equal their reports, and the decomposition agrees across providers.\n- The LP calibration reproduces the realized gain within 0.1%.\n- `--check-only`, the 3.10 grammar check and the research tests pass. Run on CPython 3.14.4; the registered 3.12 replay was not run.\n\n```sh\npython3 -I -B research/t74-entrance-raise-prices/entrance_raise.py --fetch   # ~25 s\n# PASS_T74_ENTRANCE_RAISE lp_gain=1.3166e-06 realized=1.3164e-06 best_further=+3.051e-07@k=10 own_only_k1=+3.839e-07 no_new_kappa\n```\n\n**Scope.** These are LP-ceiling prices. The average ladder assumes #2435's average partner cost. No raise is constructed; entrance delivery and Lemma A wrappers remain the open obligation, as in #2446. Base: main `0fdd7d82`. Assignment: structural-decoder track, seed 41; card `complex-rank-shape-decoder`, scope changed.\n\n**Credits.**\n- #2435 / #2374 / #2312 (Jeremy Kothe).\n- #2322 (Vlado Vojdanovski).\n- #458 (chafreaky, Lemma A).\n- #2360 (Jeremy Diviney) and #1129 (Ali Romman).\n- #2387 / #2402 / #2446 (this author): the tools, vendored with pins.\n\nPrepared with substantial AI assistance (Claude Code, Anthropic, Claude Opus 5.5). No independent human review is claimed. Apache-2.0.\n\n\ud83e\udd16 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
